Installing Percona Toolkit
==========================

System Requirements
-------------------

Most tools require:

   * Perl v5.8 or newer
   * Bash v3 or newer
   * Core Perl modules like Time::HiRes

Tools written in Go require the latest available Go version.

Tools that connect to MySQL require:

   * Perl modules DBI and DBD::mysql 5.013 or newer
   * MySQL 5.7 or newer

Percona Toolkit is only tested on UNIX systems, primarily Debian and
Red Hat derivatives; other operating systems may work but are not supported.

Tools that connect to earlier versions of MySQL may work, but this is not
tested or supported.

Installation
------------

You can install Percona Toolkit in any of the following ways:

- Install it from the Percona repository.
- Install it from a tarball.
- Build it from source.

Installing Percona Toolkit from the Percona Repository
------------------------------------------------------

1. Configure Percona repositories as described in [Percona Software Repositories Documentation](https://docs.percona.com/percona-software-repositories/index.html).

2. Enable Percona Toolkit repository:

   sudo percona-release enable pt release

3. Install Percona Toolkit using the corresponding package manager:

   - For Debian or Ubuntu:

      sudo apt-get install percona-toolkit

   - For RHEL or CentOS:

      sudo yum install percona-toolkit

Installing Percona Toolkit from a tarball
-----------------------------------------

1. Download **Linux - Generic** tarball from https://www.percona.com/downloads/

2. Extract the tarball into desired directory:

   tar -xzf percona-toolkit-M.N.P_x86_64.tar.gz

   (Replace `M.N.P` with the downloaded version number)

3. Optionally add `percona-toolkit-M.N.P/bin` directory into `$PATH` or create links to the content of the `percona-toolkit-M.N.P` directory under `/usr/local`.

Building from source
--------------------

Quick Install
-------------

   perl Makefile.PL
   make
   make test
   make install

Detailed Install
----------------

1. Getting source code.

   a. Clone Percona Toolkit from the GitHub repository at https://github.com/percona/percona-toolkit/ and cd to the resulting directory:

      git clone https://github.com/percona/percona-toolkit.git
      cd percona-toolkit

   b. Or download the tarball from the Percona Software Downloads web page at https://www.percona.com/downloads/, extract it, and cd to the resulting directory:


      tar zxvf percona-toolkit-<version>.tar.gz
      cd percona-toolkit-<version>

2. Generate the `Makefile`, which will check Perl module dependencies and
so forth:

   perl Makefile.PL

3. Build the tools' man pages and prep for test and install:

   make

4. Test that the tools can run:

   make test

   All tests should pass.  If not, then your system may be missing a Perl module
   required by a tool.  The tests are not comprehensive; they only test that the
   tools can be executed by Perl and Bash.

5. Finally, install all tools and their man pages:

   make install

   On most systems, the tools are installed in `/usr/local/bin`.

Installation Options
--------------------

To install to a directory other than your system's default, such as your
home directory, generate the Makefile with a prefix:

   perl Makefile.PL PREFIX=${HOME}